KNOWNBUG
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ both assignments: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.assign]/1: a compound assignment is an lvalue referring to its
left operand, so `(x += 2) += 3' with x a reference to b adds 5 to b.  The
goto program contains only `*x = *x + 2': the outer compound assignment is
dropped without a diagnostic (b == 3).  With x an object rather than a
reference it works.  test_parameter.desc: the same through a reference
parameter aborts symbolic execution ("goto_symext::address_arithmetic does
not handle side_effect").  Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18
accept both programs, and they fail only their WRONG assertion.
